const e="deped-national-schools-press-conference",c=2025,o="Built from the whole of the Division Memorandum (26 pages) of the Schools Division Office of Imus City for the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference. The memorandum prints no entry fee, no class or age limits, no time limit for the writing events (only schedule slots) and no judging criteria except for Mobile Journalism. The criteria for News, Editorial and Feature Writing and for Copyreading come from a blog copy of the DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet and are the ones installed in the template. No criteria are printed for Sports Writing, Science and Technology Writing, Photojournalism, Editorial Cartooning or Column Writing. The group contests, school papers and the Most Outstanding Campus Journalist awards are not items of this template, so they are summarized in the page section 'other' only. The memorandum's last page (MOCJ and MOSPA) stops after its introduction. The Division Memorandum of Sarangani in the research folder is a different division's edition and is not part of the Evidence, so it was not used.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Schools Press Conference (campus journalism). Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The 2025 Division Schools Press Conference is on {{DSPCDates}} at {{Venue}}. Pre-register online on or before {{PreRegistrationDeadline}} at {{PreRegistrationLink}}. Write NO ENTRY for categories where your school has no contestant. Each school can send one contestant for every medium (English and Filipino) in each individual event.","Notes":["Contact for questions: {{EventContact}}.","Any violation of the contest rules is a ground for disqualification.","The decisions of the Board of Judges are final and cannot be appealed.","A school that has a DSPC winner must produce a school paper, even if it does not join the school paper contest.","Check your gadgets and equipment on the dates in {{ContestTimeline}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Division Schools Press Conference (DSPC) follows Republic Act No. 7079, the Campus Journalism Act of 1991, which promotes campus journalism in schools. The Schools Division Office of Imus City holds it through its Curriculum Implementation Division.","The objectives are to equip learners with writing and technical skills for the category they join, and to prepare them for the next higher level of competition.","The participants are learner contestants and school paper advisers, in English and Filipino, from public and private schools in the Division, who join the individual and group contests.","The individual events are News Writing, Features Writing, Editorial Writing, Sports Writing, Copyreading and Headline Writing, Photojournalism, Editorial Cartooning, Column Writing, Science and Technology Writing and Mobile Journalism.","Mobile Journalism is now an official contest for Secondary only.","The group events are Radio Scriptwriting and Broadcasting, Collaborative Desktop Publishing, Online Publishing (Secondary only) and TV Scriptwriting and Broadcasting (Secondary only). The school paper events and the search for Most Outstanding Campus Journalists and School Paper Advisers are also part of the DSPC.","Each school must follow the Timeline of Campus Journalism Activities. All delegations must follow and join all activities in it.","The Division strictly follows the rules on plagiarism. An entry or school paper that copies and publishes texts, graphics or other materials without proper acknowledgment of the sources is disqualified. Any plagiarism proved by the Board of Judges in any competition is a ground for disqualification.","School heads must arrange the schedule of the affected teachers under the Department's Time-on-Task policy.","Participants who serve on Saturday 15 November 2025 get service credits under DepEd Order No. 13, s. 2024, Revised Guidelines on the Grant of Vacation Service Credits for Teachers."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Learners of public and private schools of the Division can take part, in English and in Filipino.","There are two levels: Elementary and Secondary.","Mobile Journalism is open to Secondary learners only. Each school has one representative for English and one for Filipino. They must not compete in any individual or group writing event.","Learners who join a group contest (Radio, Collaborative Desktop Publishing, Online Publishing, TV Broadcasting) must not compete in any individual writing event or in another group event.","Online Publishing and TV Broadcasting are for Secondary only.","The memorandum does not print class or age limits for the Elementary and Secondary levels.","All schools with DSPC winners must produce a school paper."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Pre-register online on or before {{PreRegistrationDeadline}}. Link: {{PreRegistrationLink}}. This is for the individual and group events.","Write NO ENTRY for categories where the school has no contestants.","Registration at the venue is from 7:00 am to 2:00 pm on Day 1 (14 November 2025) and from 7:00 to 8:00 am on Day 2 (15 November 2025).","Gadgets and equipment are checked on the dates in {{ContestTimeline}}. The memorandum lists the gadgets to check for Radio Broadcasting, Mobile Journalism and Collaborative Publishing on 13 November, and for TV Broadcasting, Online Publishing and Photojournalism on 14 November.","A school that is not complete for a team in TV or Radio Broadcasting is regrouped with other schools to make a full team of seven. If many schools still cannot form a team, the participants must give individual presentations for the selection.","For questions and clarifications contact {{EventContact}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Payment","Items":["The memorandum prints no entry fee.","The Division pays the food of the program management team, top management, materials and speakers' honoraria from the Special Education Fund (SEF).","The food and travel expenses of the participants are charged to the school MOOE or to the local or canteen fund, whichever is available."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["The 2025 Division Schools Press Conference is on {{DSPCDates}}.","The pre-registration deadline is {{PreRegistrationDeadline}}.","The Opening Program is at {{OpeningProgram}}.","The awarding ceremony is on {{AwardingCeremony}}.","The other activities (orientation, device checking, training workshops and cliniquing) are in {{ContestTimeline}}.","The day-by-day contest program is in {{ContestProgram}}."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The contests are held at {{Venue}}.","All contest rooms must have a TV or HDMI, a laptop or a USB."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Teams and Entry Limits","Items":["In the individual category, each school can send one contestant for every medium (English and Filipino) in each individual event.","In the group categories, each school can send one team with the allowed number of members for each event and medium.","Team sizes: Radio Scriptwriting and Broadcasting 7 (English and Filipino, Elementary and Secondary); Collaborative Desktop Publishing 7 (English and Filipino, Elementary and Secondary); Online Publishing 5 each for English and Filipino (Secondary); TV Scriptwriting and Broadcasting 7 each for English and Filipino (Secondary)."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Ranks","Items":["Points for each place, used for the overall standing of a school: 1st 15, 2nd 14, 3rd 13, 4th 12, 5th 11, 6th 10, 7th 9, 8th 8, 9th 7, 10th 6, 11th 5, 12th 4, 13th 3, 14th 2, 15th 1.","The points a school earns in all events, categories and levels are added to find the overall best performing schools at the Secondary and Elementary levels in the individual and group events.","All awards in the individual and group contests (except the school paper) are counted in the overall school standing.","The points of the best school papers are not added to the overall standing of schools."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Recognition","Items":["The top seven (7) winners in all individual categories are recognized at the awarding and closing ceremonies.","The top three (3) best teams in the group categories are also awarded.","All schools that have entries in the school paper contest are recognized at the awarding ceremony. Awards are announced for each section.","The 3-day training workshop for DSPC winners and the 10-day cliniquing of the best 3 winners in the individual categories and of the composite team in the group contests follow the contest. See {{ContestTimeline}}.","Special awards for Radio Broadcasting are Best Anchor, Best News Presented and Best Technical Director (individual) and Best Infomercial and Best Script (group). For TV Broadcasting they are Best Anchor, Best Director, Best Reporter and Best Technical Director (individual) and Best Developmental Communication and Best News Script (group)."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Rounds and Advancement","Items":["The Division Schools Press Conference prepares the winners for the next higher level of competition.","Only the Overall Top Five (5) Best School Papers, in English and Filipino at the Elementary and Secondary levels, represent the Division at the regional level.","A school cannot send its school paper entries directly to the Regional Office.","The Division holds cliniquing of school paper entries for the Regional Schools Press Conference (RSPC) 2026 on the dates in {{ContestTimeline}}."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct","Items":["Participants must always wear their school ID.","Participants can bring bottled water, snacks or biscuits. For events that run beyond lunch time, learners and teams must bring packed meals. Food distribution is not allowed.","Participants can raise questions and ask for help only from the assigned proctor or examiner.","School paper advisers, teachers, principals, parents or guardians found in the contest venues, including the photoshoot site for photojournalism, cause the disqualification of their contestants. Only the Program Management Team on duty can be there.","Communication devices such as cellular phones and smart gadgets are not allowed in the contest rooms, unless a specific event needs them. See the rules of the event for device checking.","Any violation of the guidelines is a ground for disqualification of the participant.","All decisions of the Board of Judges about any part of the contest are final and cannot be appealed."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Group Contests, School Papers and Other Parts of the DSPC (not in this template)","Items":["Radio Scriptwriting and Broadcasting: a team of 7 for English and 7 for Filipino at Elementary and Secondary, in plain white shirts with school ID. The team has 2 hours to write a script for a 5-minute radio broadcast (1 infomercial of at most 1 minute and 4 news reports), plus 30 minutes for printing, with up to 4 laptops, a flash drive of at most 32 GB and an inkjet printer. Virtual DJ is the official program. Each team submits 4 copies of the script (3 for the judges). The script is in Arial 12, double-spaced, on A4 paper, with no school name. Each team has 9 minutes: 3 minutes preparation, 5 minutes broadcast and 1 minute exit. Pre-recorded sound bites and voice are not allowed. Time deductions: 1-5 seconds none, 6-8 seconds 1 point, 9-25 seconds 2, 26-45 seconds 3, 46-65 seconds 4 and 66 seconds or more 5 points.","Collaborative Desktop Publishing: a team of 7 for English and Filipino at Elementary and Secondary, in a plain white shirt with school ID. The team has 4 hours for writing, layout and editing after a mini press conference and a sports event. The output is an A4 four-page full-color publication with no school marks. Each team can bring 2 DSLR cameras, 1 inkjet printer with scanner, 1 card reader, 1 blank flash drive, 2 extension wires, up to 4 laptops and art materials. Laptops are checked and labeled before the contest.","Online Publishing (Secondary only): a team of 5 for English and 5 for Filipino, in a plain white T-shirt with school ID, with a 1-hour orientation. The team has 4 hours for writing, layout, editing and uploading on the official WordPress platform. Each team uploads the URL of its output to the official portal.","TV Scriptwriting and Broadcasting (Secondary only): a team of 7 for English and 7 for Filipino. The team has 5 hours and 15 minutes for the script, shooting and editing, the infomercial and rehearsal. Each team has 19 minutes: 10 minutes for entrance and preparation, 6 minutes of broadcast and 3 minutes to exit. Time deductions come from the 5 percent time criterion: 1-20 seconds 1 point, 21-40 seconds 2, 41-60 seconds 3, 61-80 seconds 4 and 81 seconds or more 5 points. The official station names are TVB English Campus Vision and TVB Filipino CampusKonek.","School paper events (portable digital format) are open to Elementary and Secondary schools in English and Filipino. The sections are News, Editorial, Features, Sports, Science and Technology, and Layout and Page Design. The paper has 20 pages in full color (at least 3 pages for each of the News, Sports, Feature, Editorial and Science and Technology sections), size 9 x 12 inches for Elementary and 12 x 18 inches for Secondary. Plagiarism: first offense disqualification from the contest; second offense a written notice to the school head and a reprimand and a refresher course for the adviser; third offense a ban from the school paper events for three consecutive years.","School papers that qualify for the regional level are sent through the official portals with a Certificate of Circulation from the school head (noted by the Schools Division Superintendent, with the link of the school website or Facebook page), a Certificate of Endorsement signed by the Superintendent and a report on how plagiarism was prevented. The Division can disqualify entries with incomplete documents.","The Most Outstanding Campus Journalist (MOCJ) and Most Outstanding School Paper Adviser (MOSPA) awards are the most prestigious awards of the Division for Elementary and Secondary levels. They follow the guidelines and scoring system of the National Secondary School Publication Advisers Association, Inc. (NSSPAA) and the Philippine Association of Elementary Campus Paper Advisers (PAECPA)."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (SDO Imus City)","Url":"https://www.depedimuscity.com/portal/uploads/DM_683_S_2025.pdf"},{"Title":"NSPC 2024 scoring criteria (News Writing)","Url":"https://www.ilovedeped.net/2024/05/scoring-criteria-for-news-writing-at.html"}]}`),t=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.9-10, Enclosure 4 general guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each school can send one contestant for every medium (English and Filipino) in each individual event.","The top seven winners in each individual category are recognized at the awarding and closing ceremonies."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each school can send one contestant for every medium (English and Filipino) in each individual event.
- The top seven winners in each individual category are recognized at the awarding and closing ceremonies.`}],i=[{AgeGroup:"NSPC Elementary",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.9, Enclosure 4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Elementary level, in English and in Filipino.","Mobile Journalism is not held at the Elementary level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Elementary level, in English and in Filipino.
- Mobile Journalism is not held at the Elementary level.`},{AgeGroup:"NSPC Secondary",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.9, 13, Enclosure 4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Secondary level, in English and in Filipino.","Mobile Journalism is open to the Secondary level only."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Secondary level, in English and in Filipino.
- Mobile Journalism is open to the Secondary level only.`}],a=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"News Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.10-11 Specific guidelines 1, p.7-8 contest matrix; DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet as transcribed on ilovedeped.net","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":["Form and Style 40 (arrangement, lead, headline, language, coherence, transitions).","Content 50 (effective lead, key details, logical presentation, news format).","Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel)."],"Points":["Total 100 percent."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Form and Style 40 (arrangement, lead, headline, language, coherence, transitions).\\n- Content 50 (effective lead, key details, logical presentation, news format).\\n- Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel).\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100 percent."},{"Title":"Feature Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.10-11 Specific guidelines 1, p.7-8 contest matrix; DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet as transcribed on ilovedeped.net","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":["Form and Style 30 (grammar, organization, creative presentation, catchy title).","Content 60 (citing facts, new angle, imagination, balancing perspectives).","Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel)."],"Points":["Total 100 percent."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Form and Style 30 (grammar, organization, creative presentation, catchy title).\\n- Content 60 (citing facts, new angle, imagination, balancing perspectives).\\n- Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel).\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100 percent."},{"Title":"Editorial Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.10-11 Specific guidelines 1, p.7-8 contest matrix; DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet as transcribed on ilovedeped.net","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":["Form and Style 40 (lead with stand, fact-based arguments, sources, title, reasoning).","Content 50 (clear stand, factual information, understanding, logical support).","Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel)."],"Points":["Total 100 percent."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Form and Style 40 (lead with stand, fact-based arguments, sources, title, reasoning).\\n- Content 50 (clear stand, factual information, understanding, logical support).\\n- Ethics 10 (originality, citation, journalistic standards, no plagiarism or libel).\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100 percent."},{"Title":"Science and Technology Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.10-11 Specific guidelines 1, p.7-8 contest matrix","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."},{"Title":"Column Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.10-11 Specific guidelines 1, p.7-8 contest matrix","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Data sheets or other sources of information, such as a mini press conference, videos, audio recordings and photos, are given to the contestants as the basis for the article.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring clipboards and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and file holders are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."},{"Title":"Sports Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7-8, 11 Specific guidelines 2","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: from 8:00 am onwards. The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["The Program Management Team (PMT) orients the contestants and gives instructions before the contest proper.","The contestants cover an actual game.","A post-game conference is held to interview officials and athletes after the game.","The contestants go to the designated contest room to write the sports article.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room before the actual sports coverage begins.","After you submit the final article to the room facilitator, give it also to the proctor before you leave the venue.","Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo. Official scratch papers are given and are submitted to the proctor before leaving."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pen. You can also bring a clipboard and erasers (liquid and other forms)."],"NotAllowed":["Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and other materials are not allowed in the contest rooms."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: from 8:00 am onwards. The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The Program Management Team (PMT) orients the contestants and gives instructions before the contest proper.\\n- The contestants cover an actual game.\\n- A post-game conference is held to interview officials and athletes after the game.\\n- The contestants go to the designated contest room to write the sports article.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room before the actual sports coverage begins.\\n- After you submit the final article to the room facilitator, give it also to the proctor before you leave the venue.\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo. Official scratch papers are given and are submitted to the proctor before leaving.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pen. You can also bring a clipboard and erasers (liquid and other forms).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Any other materials that are not named. Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and other materials are not allowed in the contest rooms.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."},{"Title":"Copyreading and Headline Writing","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7-8, 11 Specific guidelines 3; DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet as transcribed on ilovedeped.net","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Each contestant gets one set of official contest material with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given and are submitted to the proctor before leaving.","The contestants follow the directions given in the contest piece.","The contestants provide a headline for the article."],"Allowed":["Bring your own pencil. You can also bring a sharpener, clipboard, ruler and eraser."],"NotAllowed":["Pens, markers, scissors, liquid eraser and other materials that are not named.","Writing on the back page of the contest paper.","Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes, a ruler, file holders and other materials not named in the guidelines."],"Judging":["Copyreading 60 (correct use of copyreading symbols, identifying the exact number of errors).","Headline Writing 40 (best headline selection, adherence to headline-writing standards)."],"Points":["Total 100 percent."],"Notes":["Guideline 3a lets contestants bring a ruler and guideline 3e says a ruler is not allowed. The memorandum prints both."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 11:00 am to 12:00 noon (Batch 2). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest material with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given and are submitted to the proctor before leaving.\\n- The contestants follow the directions given in the contest piece.\\n- The contestants provide a headline for the article.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own pencil. You can also bring a sharpener, clipboard, ruler and eraser.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pens, markers, scissors, liquid eraser and other materials that are not named.\\n- Writing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes, a ruler, file holders and other materials not named in the guidelines.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Copyreading 60 (correct use of copyreading symbols, identifying the exact number of errors).\\n- Headline Writing 40 (best headline selection, adherence to headline-writing standards).\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100 percent.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Guideline 3a lets contestants bring a ruler and guideline 3e says a ruler is not allowed. The memorandum prints both."},{"Title":"Editorial Cartooning","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7-8, 12 Specific guidelines 4","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit."],"Rules":["Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.","Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.","The cartoon must be based on the given topic or issue.","The cartoon must follow the professional and ethical standards of media."],"Allowed":["Bring your own Mongol No. 2 pencil. You can also bring a sharpener, ruler, clipboard and eraser."],"NotAllowed":["Pens, markers, scissors, liquid eraser and other materials that are not named.","Drawing on the back page of the contest paper.","Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and other materials not named in the guidelines."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: 9:30 to 10:30 am (Batch 1). The memorandum prints no separate time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each contestant gets one set of official contest papers with the official DSPC logo.\\n- Official scratch papers are given in the contest room. Give them to the proctor before you leave.\\n- The cartoon must be based on the given topic or issue.\\n- The cartoon must follow the professional and ethical standards of media.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own Mongol No. 2 pencil. You can also bring a sharpener, ruler, clipboard and eraser.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pens, markers, scissors, liquid eraser and other materials that are not named.\\n- Drawing on the back page of the contest paper.\\n- Other sheets of paper, folders, envelopes and other materials not named in the guidelines.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."},{"Title":"Photojournalism","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7-8, 12-13 Specific guidelines 5","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Schedule on 15 November: from 8:00 am onwards.","Be at the contest venue 30 minutes before the orientation.","One hour to take pictures. Then 30 minutes to write the captions."],"Rules":["Use point-and-shoot digital single-lens reflex (DSLR) cameras with an 18-55 mm f/3.5-5.6 lens.","Submit a clear (empty) memory card and the camera (internal memory) to the technical experts for checking on the scheduled date. Checking of gadgets for Photojournalism is on 14 November.","Load the empty storage card in front of the examiner on the contest day. The loading and unloading of the storage card is done in front of the examiner.","The control shot must be the first shot.","You can take unlimited shots but you submit only four possible photos with captions for the given theme and the control shot.","Write the file name of each photo on the caption sheet. The PMT gives the caption sheets."],"Allowed":["Bring your own camera cable and/or card reader for uploading and saving pictures.","Bring your own black ink ballpen. The PMT gives official scratch papers for notes during the shooting."],"NotAllowed":["Cameras with higher specifications. Mirrorless cameras are strictly not allowed.","Cellular phones, smart gadgets and devices, extra digital cameras, extra storage cards or any additional materials or equipment in the contest area.","School paper advisers, teachers, principals, parents and guardians at the photoshoot site. Their contestants are disqualified."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Schedule on 15 November: from 8:00 am onwards.\\n- Be at the contest venue 30 minutes before the orientation.\\n- One hour to take pictures. Then 30 minutes to write the captions.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Use point-and-shoot digital single-lens reflex (DSLR) cameras with an 18-55 mm f/3.5-5.6 lens.\\n- Submit a clear (empty) memory card and the camera (internal memory) to the technical experts for checking on the scheduled date. Checking of gadgets for Photojournalism is on 14 November.\\n- Load the empty storage card in front of the examiner on the contest day. The loading and unloading of the storage card is done in front of the examiner.\\n- The control shot must be the first shot.\\n- You can take unlimited shots but you submit only four possible photos with captions for the given theme and the control shot.\\n- Write the file name of each photo on the caption sheet. The PMT gives the caption sheets.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Bring your own camera cable and/or card reader for uploading and saving pictures.\\n- Bring your own black ink ballpen. The PMT gives official scratch papers for notes during the shooting.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Cameras with higher specifications. Mirrorless cameras are strictly not allowed.\\n- Cellular phones, smart gadgets and devices, extra digital cameras, extra storage cards or any additional materials or equipment in the contest area.\\n- School paper advisers, teachers, principals, parents and guardians at the photoshoot site. Their contestants are disqualified.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The memorandum does not print the judging criteria for this event."},{"Title":"Mobile Journalism","Source":"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7, 13-14 Specific guidelines 6","Sections":{"About":["Mobile Journalism is an official contest for Secondary only."],"TimeAndFormat":["The contest is on 14 November (Day 1). Gadgets are checked on 13 November from 8:00 am to 2:00 pm.","A 20-minute orientation comes before the contest.","A 30-minute mini press conference gives the content for the entries.","Three hours for production: writing, shooting, voice recording and editing. Interviews and the mini press conference are not part of the 3 hours.","30 minutes to upload the entry to the official portal. The access link is given on the contest day after the 3 hours.","The video is a news-style entry of 2 to 3 minutes, vertical or horizontal, in .mp4 or .mov."],"Rules":["Each school has one representative for English and one for Filipino at the Secondary level. They must not compete in any individual or group writing event.","All contestants attend the orientation. Official paper is given, and contestants bring their own pen.","Contestants cannot go back to their quarters or communicate in any form (text, call, chat and so on) with their advisers from the start to the end of the contest.","The mobile application is CapCut (free version, not premium).","Social media applications, email and other communication channels must be uninstalled from the phones.","Each participant can ask only one question (no follow-up) to the resource person at the mini press conference.","Participants can use the internet through a Wi-Fi modem for research. They must not use any downloaded material as content in any part of the output.","The script is not evaluated but is given to the proctor after the time allotment.","Official mobile phones, cleared of stored documents, files and applications, are given to the PMT during the checking of devices. If you do not submit on or before the deadline you are disqualified.","Not following the guidelines means disqualification.","Wear smart casual attire with no identifying marks or logos of the school."],"Allowed":["Each contestant can bring only: 1 mobile phone (Android or iOS) and a charger that fits it (without SIM or eSIM card); 1 cord for data or file transfer; 1 power bank; 1 monopod; 1 tripod; 1 portable microphone; 1 portable light; and a maximum of 2 WiFi routers or pocket WiFi, preferably with different networks."],"NotAllowed":["Mobile data for the internet.","Glam teams are strictly not allowed.","Going back to quarters or contacting advisers during the contest."],"Judging":["Use of mobile journalism principles, done entirely with the mobile device, 40: Shooting 10, Recording 10, Writing 10, Editing 10.","Accuracy of the Mobile Journalism piece 40: Fact-checking and Sources 8, Cross-Verification 8, Contextual Understanding 8, Transparency 8, Editorial Standards 8.","Maintaining broadcast quality output 20: Technical Standards 5, Production Values 5, Adherence to Style Guidelines 5, Engagement and Audience Experience 5."],"Points":["Total 100 percent."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Mobile Journalism is an official contest for Secondary only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The contest is on 14 November (Day 1). Gadgets are checked on 13 November from 8:00 am to 2:00 pm.\\n- A 20-minute orientation comes before the contest.\\n- A 30-minute mini press conference gives the content for the entries.\\n- Three hours for production: writing, shooting, voice recording and editing. Interviews and the mini press conference are not part of the 3 hours.\\n- 30 minutes to upload the entry to the official portal. The access link is given on the contest day after the 3 hours.\\n- The video is a news-style entry of 2 to 3 minutes, vertical or horizontal, in .mp4 or .mov.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school has one representative for English and one for Filipino at the Secondary level. They must not compete in any individual or group writing event.\\n- All contestants attend the orientation. Official paper is given, and contestants bring their own pen.\\n- Contestants cannot go back to their quarters or communicate in any form (text, call, chat and so on) with their advisers from the start to the end of the contest.\\n- The mobile application is CapCut (free version, not premium).\\n- Social media applications, email and other communication channels must be uninstalled from the phones.\\n- Each participant can ask only one question (no follow-up) to the resource person at the mini press conference.\\n- Participants can use the internet through a Wi-Fi modem for research. They must not use any downloaded material as content in any part of the output.\\n- The script is not evaluated but is given to the proctor after the time allotment.\\n- Official mobile phones, cleared of stored documents, files and applications, are given to the PMT during the checking of devices. If you do not submit on or before the deadline you are disqualified.\\n- Not following the guidelines means disqualification.\\n- Wear smart casual attire with no identifying marks or logos of the school.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Each contestant can bring only: 1 mobile phone (Android or iOS) and a charger that fits it (without SIM or eSIM card); 1 cord for data or file transfer; 1 power bank; 1 monopod; 1 tripod; 1 portable microphone; 1 portable light; and a maximum of 2 WiFi routers or pocket WiFi, preferably with different networks.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Mobile data for the internet.\\n- Glam teams are strictly not allowed.\\n- Going back to quarters or contacting advisers during the contest.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Use of mobile journalism principles, done entirely with the mobile device, 40: Shooting 10, Recording 10, Writing 10, Editing 10.\\n- Accuracy of the Mobile Journalism piece 40: Fact-checking and Sources 8, Cross-Verification 8, Contextual Understanding 8, Transparency 8, Editorial Standards 8.\\n- Maintaining broadcast quality output 20: Technical Standards 5, Production Values 5, Adherence to Style Guidelines 5, Engagement and Audience Experience 5.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Total 100 percent."}]'),r=[],s=[{Key:"DSPCDates",Kind:"date",Label:"DSPC dates",Value:"14-15 November 2025",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.1"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"Imus National High School",Address:"Imus City, Cavite",City:"Imus City, Cavite",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.1"},{Key:"PreRegistrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to pre-register",Value:"2025-11-05",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.2 item 6"},{Key:"PreRegistrationLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Online pre-registration form",Value:"https://tinyurl.com/Reg-DSPC2025",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.2 item 6"},{Key:"OpeningProgram",Kind:"time",Label:"Opening Program",Value:"14 November 2025 at 8:00 am, Imus National High School",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.5, 7"},{Key:"AwardingCeremony",Kind:"text",Label:"Awarding ceremony",Value:"19 November 2025 at 1:00 pm. The timeline says the venue is to be announced and the activity matrix says GEANHS (Gen. Emilio Aguinaldo National High School).",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.6-7"},{Key:"ContestTimeline",Kind:"text",Label:"Timeline of campus journalism activities",Value:"7 November 2025, 1 pm: orientation of PMTs and TWGs at Imus National High School. 13 November 2025, 8 am to 2 pm only: checking of gadgets and equipment for Radio Broadcasting, Mobile Journalism and Collaborative Publishing, and rehearsal for the radio station. 14 November 2025, from 7 am: contest proper for Collaborative Publishing, Radio Broadcasting and Mobile Journalism; checking of gadgets for TV Broadcasting, Online Publishing and Photojournalism from 8 am to 2 pm; rehearsal for the TV mock studio. 15 November 2025, from 7 am: contest proper for all individual categories, TV Broadcasting and Online Publishing. 19 November 2025, 1 pm: awarding ceremony (venue to be announced). 20-22 November 2025, from 8 am: 3-day training workshop for DSPC winners (venue to be announced). 1-12 December 2025, from 8 am: 10-day cliniquing of the best 3 winners in the individual categories and the composite team in the group contests (venue to be announced). 16-18 December 2025, from 8 am: Division cliniquing of school paper entries for RSPC 2026 (venue to be announced).",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.6"},{Key:"ContestProgram",Kind:"text",Label:"Contest program by day",Value:"Day 0, 13 November: checking of gadgets and equipment (7:00 am to 2:00 pm only). Day 1, 14 November: registration and release of gadgets for Radio Broadcasting, Mobile Journalism and Collaborative Publishing 7:00 am to 2:00 pm; opening program 8:01 to 9:00 am; checking of gadgets for TV Broadcasting, Online Publishing and Photojournalism 9:01 am to 2:00 pm; contest proper for Collaborative Desktop Publishing, Radio Broadcasting and Mobile Journalism. Day 2, 15 November: registration and release of gadgets for TV Broadcasting, Online Publishing and Photojournalism 7:00 to 8:00 am; from 8:00 am contest proper for TV Broadcasting, Online Publishing, Sports Writing and Photojournalism; break 9:01 to 9:30 (individual contests only); 9:30 to 10:30 am Batch 1: Editorial Writing, Column Writing, Feature Writing and Editorial Cartooning; 11:00 am to 12:00 noon Batch 2: Science Writing, Copyreading and Headline Writing and News Writing. The contest matrix page heads the individual contest rooms with 14 November. The activity matrix puts the individual contests on 15 November.",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.7-8"},{Key:"EventContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact for questions",Value:{Name:"Ricardo R. David III",Role:"Education Program Supervisor in English, in charge of Campus Journalism in English",Phone:"(046) 419-8450 local 221",WhatsApp:"",Email:"imus.city@deped.gov.ph"},Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.2 item 9"},{Key:"DivisionOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Schools Division Office of Imus City",Value:{Name:"Schools Division Office of Imus City, Curriculum Implementation Division",Role:"Toclong I-C, Imus City, Cavite. Website www.depedimuscity.com. Facebook @sdoimuscity",Phone:"(046) 4198450 to 53",WhatsApp:"",Email:"imus.city@deped.gov.ph"},Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.1"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the memorandum",Value:[{Date:"2025-10-01",Title:"2025 Division Schools Press Conference announced",Text:"The Schools Division Office of Imus City announces the 2025 DSPC on 14-15 November 2025 at Imus National High School. Pre-register online before 5 November 2025.",Url:"https://www.depedimuscity.com/portal/uploads/DM_683_S_2025.pdf"}],Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025), p.1-2"}],l=[{Claim:"DSPC dates, venue, pre-registration, individual event guidelines, general rules, points per placing and recognition.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own memorandum",Source:"SDO Imus City Division Memorandum, Conduct of the 2025 Division Schools Press Conference (DM 683 s. 2025)",Url:"https://www.depedimuscity.com/portal/uploads/DM_683_S_2025.pdf"},{Claim:"Judging criteria of News, Editorial, Feature Writing and Copyreading (Mobile Journalism criteria are printed in the memorandum).",SourceType:"Secondary - blog transcription of the DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet",Source:"DepEd NSPC 2024 scoresheet as transcribed on ilovedeped.net",Url:"https://www.ilovedeped.net/2024/05/scoring-criteria-for-news-writing-at.html"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:o,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,o as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,c as Year,d as default};
